# JDK 27 RUN AS CLOSE TO JDK 25 AS IT CAN BE, for BOTH apps (web: G1, worker: Serial).
#
# Derived on 2026-09-27 by running every prod JAVA_OPTS (web base + US, all five workers) under
# Temurin 25.0.4.1+1 (what prod ran) and Temurin 27+35 on k3s-worker-1 itself, and diffing every
# final flag value (-XX:+PrintFlagsFinal with diagnostic+experimental unlocked), every system
# property and every security setting. Each line below is one difference, set back to 25's value;
# JdkParityOptionsSpec re-runs the JVM with these options and holds the result to 25's values.
#
# What cannot be put back (no flag restores it) is left as 27 ships it: G1's new card-table
# refinement (JEP 522: G1PerThreadPendingCardThreshold replaces the removed G1UpdateBufferSize),
# G1's split array marking (ArrayMarkingMinStride), C2's reachability-fence nodes and its new
# interference-graph bailout (IFGEdgesLimit). New 27 flags whose default already IS 25's behaviour
# (LoopPeeling=1, DelayAfterInliningCutoff, HotCodeHeap, NMethodRelocation, AOT*) need no line.
# The G1CPUUsage*/G1ShrinkByPercentOfAvailable resizing flags are inert: every pod runs Xms == Xmx.

# JEP 534 (27): compact object headers became the default.
-XX:-UseCompactObjectHeaders

# Diagnostic flags below need unlocking; the worker's JAVA_OPTS unlock them too, web's do not.
-XX:+UnlockDiagnosticVMOptions
# 27 turned on the side table for inflated monitors.
-XX:-UseObjectMonitorTable
# Renamed from LightweightFastLockingSpins (25: 13) with a new default of 8.
-XX:FastLockingSpins=13
# 27 enables the ML-DSA (Dilithium) intrinsics on this CPU; 25 did not.
-XX:-UseDilithiumIntrinsics
# New C2 loop and vectorization optimizations in 26/27; off is 25's code shape.
-XX:-ShortRunningLongLoop
-XX:-UseAutoVectorizationPredicate
-XX:-UseAutoVectorizationSpeculativeAliasingChecks

# Heap-sizing and allocation-prefetch ergonomics that changed. InitialRAMPercentage is inert while
# Xms is set, but it is a difference. The prefetch values are what 25 chose on k3s-worker-1's
# Skylake Xeon; a different CPU would have had its own.
-XX:InitialRAMPercentage=1.5625
-XX:AllocatePrefetchDistance=256
-XX:AllocatePrefetchLines=3

# JEP 527 (27): X25519MLKEM768 went to the front of the TLS 1.3 key-share list, and ffdhe6144/8192
# left it. This is 25's list exactly. Protocols, cipher suites and signature schemes are unchanged.
-Djdk.tls.namedGroups=x25519,secp256r1,secp384r1,secp521r1,x448,ffdhe2048,ffdhe3072,ffdhe4096,ffdhe6144,ffdhe8192
